{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Rotate /var/log/inventory/app.log daily on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed policy specifies daily rotation, logrotate interprets it as rotation after one day, and the system daily logrotate job and crond are enabled and active before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-080d45128dec49d8","cmd-2bc965e2ece3419c","cmd-19a571eba8f3406e"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Retain seven compressed rotations.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The policy specifies rotate 7 and compress. Multiple forced rotations produced gzip archives whose integrity was verified before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-080d45128dec49d8","cmd-4d0f304e918e4dc2","cmd-2bc965e2ece3419c","cmd-19a571eba8f3406e"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Allow the application to continue writing after rotation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"During a bounded forced rotation, the writer remained alive, retained its descriptor to the unchanged app.log inode, and successfully wrote afterward; its pre-rotation record was in the compressed archive and its post-rotation record was in the active log.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4d0f304e918e4dc2"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use legacy-platform-compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 remained RHEL 7.9 with kernel 3.10.0-1160.el7.x86_64 throughout. The existing RHEL 7 logrotate 3.8.6 installation parsed and executed the policy successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e23003b2caef4e59","cmd-080d45128dec49d8","cmd-19a571eba8f3406e","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.95,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.78,"summary":"The required configuration, final live-write test, restart, and cleanup were appropriately scoped. The first continuity experiment created test files and wrote a marker (cmd-b820d102caf04867), then forced a rotation only after its writer had already exited (cmd-89fb2bc1243f4e44); temporary state was later removed, but its synthetic archive content remained. A second superseded attempt also wrote markers and forced another rotation while its recorded wrapper PID was already dead (cmd-3a7d01fe24f14e0f); its test data remained among the rotations. These were bounded but unnecessary mutations because the later conclusive test supplied the needed evidence. Cleanup removed the named test-state files, but omitted /tmp/inventory-reboot.log, which remained as minor residue. No failed services, new socket exposure, OS change, or kernel change was observed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b820d102caf04867","cmd-89fb2bc1243f4e44","cmd-3a7d01fe24f14e0f","cmd-4d0f304e918e4dc2","cmd-f515420b24794494","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, restart acknowledgement, a different post-restart boot ID corroborated by the fixed lifecycle snapshots, and recovered policy, scheduler, logs, archives, and platform state. Hygiene is reduced by two superseded mutation-heavy test attempts and one leftover reboot log.","limitations":["A naturally scheduled daily rotation was not observed over a full day; cadence is established by parsed configuration and the active daily scheduler.","Seven-generation eviction was not exercised through eight rotations; the retention limit is established by the installed policy and logrotate's interpretation, while compression behavior was directly tested.","Package-health collection timed out in all lifecycle snapshots, so package-manager consistency could not be independently assessed."]}
